      "body": "\n\n\n\n## Overview\nFix FP8 attention metadata in both Pixtral vision towers so FlashInfer uses correct buffer offsets for batches containing multiple images.\n\n\n## Claims\n- Pass the FP8 padded hidden size through Pixtral’s packed sequence metadata generation.\n- Use matching Q/K/V offsets for separately quantized FP8 buffers, avoiding out-of-bounds V reads.\n- Preserve the existing non-FP8 metadata behavior.\n\n\n## Validation\n\nNeeds Blackwell (SM 100+); FP8 ViT attention isn't supported on Hopper.\n\n  ```bash\n  vllm serve mistralai/Pixtral-12B-2409 --tokenizer-mode mistral \\\n    --mm-encoder-attn-backend FLASHINFER --mm-encoder-attn-dtype fp8 \\\n    --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\": 1}' --max-model-len 8192\n  ```\n\n  Then send ~16 concurrent chat requests, each with a different 1024x768 image (a single request may not trigger it).\n\n  - Before: the engine core crashes with `CUDA error: an illegal memory access`; the in-flight and subsequent requests return 500 (`EngineDeadError`). \n  -  After: all requests return 200.\n\n\n## Details\nFlashInfer FP8 attention quantizes Q/K/V into separate contiguous buffers. Pixtral omitted the FP8 padded hidden size when generating metadata, causing V offsets to retain the packed-QKV layout’s 3x stride. For subsequent images, these offsets can point beyond the V buffer.\nBoth vision towers now resolve the padded hidden size during construction and pass it through metadata generation, reusing the existing FP8 offset handling.\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63713?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795600061&installation_model_id=425286&pr_number=63713&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=vllm-project%2Fvllm&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fvllm-project%2Fvllm%2Fpull%2F63713&signature=89b25b417e8ad712aba119cfd07eb7c751bce92cf9d0aaa3429bd0cad4a8d95f\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
